WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.716
Now read the full assigned case, For This We Get a
Master's Degree?, in Canvas.

2
00:00:04.916 --> 00:00:12.208
At Handgrove College Library, reference librarians raise
concerns about repeatedly handling computer and printer
problems.

3
00:00:12.408 --> 00:00:15.916
Joan Cloud is the director; Louise Reid heads reference.

4
00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:20.782
Dana Warne narrates the meeting with colleagues Miriam
Bindloss and Gilbert Vedder.

5
00:00:20.982 --> 00:00:24.189
The case ends without a final management decision.

6
00:00:24.389 --> 00:00:29.645
A suggestion that Joan might consult colleagues is an
expectation, not a confirmed event.

7
00:00:29.845 --> 00:00:36.230
Consider two time perspectives: what planning might have
prevented the situation, and what the library should do
now.

8
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.255
Begin with reported facts and missing information.

9
00:00:39.455 --> 00:00:44.436
Identify service needs, affected people, feasible
alternatives, and tradeoffs.

10
00:00:44.636 --> 00:00:48.579
Explain how your recommendation would be implemented and
evaluated.

11
00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:51.167
Use Chapter Four as the central lens.

12
00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:56.198
Connect maintenance coordination or service expectations
only when relevant.

13
00:00:56.398 --> 00:01:00.781
Do not invent a budget, an IT department, policies, or a
resolution.

14
00:01:00.981 --> 00:01:06.541
Treat technical and support work respectfully, and
distinguish the narrator's judgments from evidence.

15
00:01:06.741 --> 00:01:09.798
Canvas has the discussion requirements and deadline.

16
00:01:09.998 --> 00:01:13.122
The optional game follows; it has no grade impact.

17
00:01:13.322 --> 00:01:15.624
Your case analysis remains your own.

